ty of Ur and took its last king, Ibbi-Sin, captive.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/elamites"><span class="enc-name">Elamites</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Elamites were the people of ancient Elam in south-western Iran, who formed the Elamite Confederation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elateia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elateia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elateia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elateia was the largest city of ancient Phocis in central Greece, in the Cephissus valley, commanding the route from Thessaly into Boeotia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elazig"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elazig.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elazığ</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elazığ is a city in eastern Anatolia, Turkey, on a plain east of the Euphrates.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elba</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elba is the largest island of the Tuscan Archipelago, off the coast of Tuscany, Italy, facing Piombino.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elbasan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elbasan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elbasan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elbasan is a city in central Albania on the Shkumbin river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elbe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elbe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elbe</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Elbe is a major river of central Europe, about 1,100 km long, rising in the Giant Mountains of the Czech Republic and flowing through Germany to the North Sea below…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elbe-germanic-peoples"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elbe-germanic-peoples.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elbe Germanic peoples</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Elbe Germanic peoples are a group of early Germanic peoples defined by archaeologists and historians in the Elbe basin, broadly matching the Irminones of Roman…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elberfeld"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elberfeld.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elberfeld</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elberfeld is a former town in the Wupper valley of western Germany, joined with Barmen and neighbouring towns in 1929 to form the city later named Wuppertal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elbistan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elbistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elbistan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elbistan is a town in Kahramanmaraş Province, south-eastern Turkey, on a high plain of the eastern Taurus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elblag"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elblag.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elbląg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elbląg is a city in northern Poland near the Vistula Lagoon.</span></a></li></ul>
